# Use the image CMD instead of replacing it with `sleep infinity`.
#
# The Dockerfile CMD boots Elasticsearch (backgrounded, as the elasticsearch
# user) with X-Pack security disabled, then execs `sleep infinity`, so:
#   * the daemon is ALREADY RUNNING with an open, unauthenticated REST API when
#     the agent starts, which makes the "enabled security in the config but
#     never restarted" case detectable (the live node still answers 200 to
#     anonymous requests);
#   * PID 1 is still `sleep infinity`, so restarting ES cannot kill the
#     container.
#
# Consequence for solutions: the fix must enable xpack.security, provision the
# elastic user password, AND RESTART Elasticsearch.  ES boots in ~40s; wait for
# readiness after restart.
